        "id": "about_chapter_13-1",
        "text": "Subsecciones de: Chapter 13: Python and Machine Learning\nP\u00e1ginas: 456-481\n\u2022 Technical requirements  (457)\n\u2022 Introducing machine learning  (457)\n\u2022 Using Python for machine learning  (460)\n  \u2022 Introducing machine learning libraries in Python  (460)\n  \u2022 Best practices of training data with Python  (462)\n\u2022 Building and evaluating a machine learning model  (462)\n  \u2022 Learning about an ML model building process  (463)\n  \u2022 Building a sample ML model  (464)\n  \u2022 Evaluating a model using cross-validation and fine tuning hyperparameters  (470)\n  \u2022 Saving an ML model to a file  (474)\n\u2022 Deploying and predicting an ML model on GCP Cloud  (475)\n\u2022 Summary  (478)\n\u2022 Questions  (479)\n\u2022 Further reading  (479)\n\u2022 Answers  (480)\n13\nPython and\nMachine Learning\nMachine learning ( ML ) is a branch of artificial intelligence ( AI ) that is based on\nbuilding models by learning patterns from data and then using those models to make\npredictions. It is one of the most popular AI techniques for helping humans as well as\nbusinesses in many ways. For example, it is being used for medical diagnosis, image\nprocessing, speech recognition, predicting threats, data mining, classification, and many\nmore scenarios. We all understand the importance and usefulness of machine learning\nin our lives. Python, being a concise but powerful language, is being used extensively to\nimplement machine learning models. Python's ability to process and prepare data using\nlibraries such as NumPy, pandas, and PySpark makes it a preferred choice for developers\nfor building and training ML models.\nIn this chapter, we will discuss using Python for machine learning tasks in an optimized\nway. This is especially important because training an ML model is a compute-intensive\ntask and optimizing the code is fundamental when using Python for machine learning.\n434     Python and Machine Learning\nWe will cover the following topics in this chapter:\n\u2022I Introducing machine learning\n\u2022I Using Python for machine learning\n\u2022I Testing and evaluating machine learning models\n\u2022I Deploying machine learning models in the cloud",
